  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "editcap: fix buffer overread in --sctp-split for truncated captures",
  "description": "When processing packets where caplen < len (e.g., snaplen-limited\ncaptures), sctp_split_and_write() used chunk_len from the SCTP chunk\nheader to memcpy data from the packet buffer. Since chunk_len reflects\nthe full on-wire size, this read beyond the captured data into\nuninitialized memory.\n\nFix by calculating the actually captured portion of each chunk and:\n- Only copying chunk_captured bytes (min of chunk_len and available data)\n- Setting caplen to reflect the truncated size\n- Keeping len at the full on-wire size\n\nThis preserves the \"Packet size limited during capture\" annotation in\noutput files and prevents undefined behavior.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Kiro)",
